---
description: Agent security rules for setup, shell commands, and secrets handling
alwaysApply: true
---

`docs/SECURITY.md` owns security policy. Read its affected sections before
install/setup, executable validation, shell use, or auth/private-data work.

Never expose secrets or use remote pipe-to-shell. Review repository executable
inputs against a trusted base before host execution; otherwise use exact-SHA
disposable credential-free isolation. A worktree alone is not isolation.
Destructive commands require explicit authority. Production database access and
agent-executed account deletion in every environment are forbidden.
Shell payload handling, install approvals, and auth/session invariants live in
the canonical owner; retrieve them for the affected operation.
